WEBVTT

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.830
Yamazaki-san.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.440
Good morning.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.120
Hey. Good morning.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:18.220
You're up pretty early.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:21.370
Yeah. I've been kind of on edge lately.

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:24.120
You're up early yourself, though.

00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:27.250
I'm feeling pretty anxious, 
too, to be honest...

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:28.880
Huh?

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.030
There's something on your shoulder.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:38.760
Yeah...

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:41.110
It's getting to be that time.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.390
<i>Autumn.</i>

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:49.400
<i>A time when all men in black at 
Teiai become slightly nervous.</i>

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:51.900
<i>That time of the year.</i>

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:55.320
What the hell is this report?

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.650
Not only is the information organized terribly,

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:00.740
but there are some 
unthinkable typos, too.

00:01:01.190 --> 00:01:01.930
Look here.

00:01:02.180 --> 00:01:06.000
<b>President Hyoudou</b>

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:06.000
You spelled President Hyoudou's 
name as "Byoudou," like "equality"!

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:06.000
<b>President Byoudou (Equality)</b>

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:10.100
You know he hates that 
word more than any other!

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.410
I-I'm sorry!

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:17.640
<b>Twitch... Twitch... Twitch...</b>

00:01:19.480 --> 00:01:21.640
Honestly, you people...

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:32.000
<i>Autumn. The season of personnel transfers.</i>

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.860
<i>The men in black, even Tonegawa,</i>

00:01:35.210 --> 00:01:38.700
<i>are ultimately insignificant office 
workers employed by the Teiai Group.</i>

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:43.270
<i>And one thing they cannot avoid... 
are personnel transfers.</i>

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:54.170
<b>Middle Management Blues</b>

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:54.170
<b><i>Mr. Tonegawa</i></b>

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:17.500
<b>Smoking room</b>

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:19.760
<i>Agenda 17
</i><b>\h\h\hUnofficial Announcement</b>

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:21.090
Hey, Yamazaki.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:22.570
Kikuchi-san?

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:33.230
So, you hear anything?

00:03:34.230 --> 00:03:36.570
Wh-What do you mean?

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:38.730
Come on, man.

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:40.490
About transfers.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:42.820
<b>Psst...</b>

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:48.820
<i>At Teiai, on October 1st, a meeting is 
held to decide on personnel transfers.</i>

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:46.470
Oct. 1  Meeting (Management)

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:49.510
Oct. 1  Personnel Changes

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:53.500
<i>And then, for the following two weeks, 
the information is meted out internally.</i>

00:03:50.140 --> 00:03:50.970
Oct. 15  Unofficial Announcements

00:03:52.430 --> 00:03:54.000
Oct. 31  Announcements Concluded

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:58.770
<i>The calls come down to the transfers, 
straight from human resources.</i>

00:04:03.350 --> 00:04:06.840
<i>Until that time, 
the transfers are confidential.</i>

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:11.490
<i>Only the chosen among the higher-ups 
are privy to these secrets.</i>

00:04:12.020 --> 00:04:15.510
<i>But no matter how tightly 
information is tamped down,</i>

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:19.350
<i>every time, like clockwork... 
there are leaks.</i>

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:25.380
<i>Shockingly enough, 
sometimes from management.</i>

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.280
This is just between you and me...

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:31.290
<i>But it never ends there!</i>

00:04:32.770 --> 00:04:34.700
<i>Information transmits, disseminates,</i>

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:36.040
<i>like a pandemic,</i>

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:39.650
<i>across a veritable black network!</i>

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.000
<i>But...</i>

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:43.670
Well, Yamazaki?

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:49.680
W-Well, I haven't managed to 
hear anything this time around.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:51.050
I know, right?

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:55.440
I've had my ear to the ground this time, 
but I haven't turned up anything!

00:04:56.490 --> 00:04:58.970
<i>Of course not. No one would tell you...</i>

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:04.280
<i>that you're the one being 
shipped out, Kikuchi-san!</i>

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:04.850
<i>Indeed.</i>

00:05:04.850 --> 00:05:06.010
<i>Psst...</i>

00:05:06.010 --> 00:05:08.250
<i>News of personnel changes may spread,</i>

00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:10.410
<i>but they never reach the parties affected.</i>

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:11.480
<i>Psst...</i>

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:14.950
<i>It's a quietly observed line in the sand, 
the etiquette of working adults.</i>

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.330
<i>Thus, naturally...</i>

00:05:17.700 --> 00:05:19.460
Well, I'm heading back.

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:22.610
<i>Things get awkward. Distance is maintained.</i>

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:21.000
Yeah.

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:25.970
<i>The only one who don't know 
are the ones affected.</i>

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:25.970
<b>Smoking Room</b>

00:05:27.220 --> 00:05:29.970
<i>It's the Men in Black Donut Phenomenon!</i>

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:33.970
<i>Days later...</i>

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:40.900
<i>I came because he said 
it was important, but...</i>

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.230
Sorry for the wait.

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:44.490
I've already got seats for us.

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:45.990
Okay...

00:05:47.640 --> 00:05:51.220
<i>What would he want to talk 
about at a time like this?</i>

00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:06.610
This is the first time we've gone out 
for drinks alone, right, Kikuchi-san?

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:08.330
Alone?

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:13.840
Hey, Yamazaki.

00:06:13.840 --> 00:06:14.770
<i>Psst...</i>

00:06:15.510 --> 00:06:16.920
Good to see you.

00:06:16.920 --> 00:06:18.270
Hagio-san?

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:20.280
Have a seat, man.

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:21.150
<i>Psst...</i>

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:23.900
Nagata-san!

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:27.650
<b>Shudder Shudder Shudder</b>

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:27.650
<i>He's chilled!</i>

00:06:28.340 --> 00:06:33.010
<i>Seeing this trio, 
Yamazaki is understandably shaken.</i>

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:34.680
<i>The reason being...</i>

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:39.790
<i>The members of Team Tonegawa 
being transferred out are...</i>

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:41.290
<i>Kikuchi...</i>

00:06:41.730 --> 00:06:42.790
<i>Hagio...</i>

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:45.050
<i>and Nagata!</i>

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.830
Cheers!

00:06:47.830 --> 00:06:49.550
<i>These three men.</i>

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:56.060
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:56.060
<i>C-Could info about their 
transfers have leaked to them?</i>

00:06:56.530 --> 00:07:01.010
<i>N-No way. Even if it did, 
why would they call me?</i>

00:07:01.010 --> 00:07:02.810
S-So...

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:06.320
How do I put this?

00:07:06.690 --> 00:07:10.070
Th-This is an odd lineup, isn't it?

00:07:11.140 --> 00:07:12.330
You think so?

00:07:12.330 --> 00:07:15.100
But we meet up two or three 
times a month, don't we?

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.080
We sure do.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.900
Y-You must be good friends.

00:07:21.620 --> 00:07:25.740
It's not so much that. 
More like... we're comrades.

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:27.370
Like a study group.

00:07:27.780 --> 00:07:29.210
What it boils down to is...

00:07:29.210 --> 00:07:34.970
We all have the same goal in mind: 
changing Teiai for the better.

00:07:36.020 --> 00:07:37.550
<i>Th-This is...</i>

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.470
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:40.330
Let me ask you, Yamazaki.

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:44.230
Do you really think Teiai should 
keep operating the way it does now?

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:46.240
<i>You gotta be kidding me...</i>

00:07:45.670 --> 00:07:47.480
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:07:48.050 --> 00:07:51.350
If we're always waiting on the president to 
make the call, with top-down decision making,

00:07:51.350 --> 00:07:53.830
the company won't survive.

00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:57.120
<i>No, I'm sure of it. These three...</i>

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:03.790
<i>They're colluding! Without knowing 
they're about to be moved!</i>

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:05.040
Yamazaki.

00:08:07.350 --> 00:08:10.330
We think you have potential.

00:08:10.330 --> 00:08:12.890
And Team Tonegawa has a lot 
of forward momentum right now.

00:08:12.890 --> 00:08:16.640
With us at the core, we can 
change Teiai for the better!

00:08:16.640 --> 00:08:22.390
And in time, I'll assume the role of Teiai's 
number two man for Tonegawa-sensei!

00:08:22.390 --> 00:08:24.400
No, it'll be me!

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.940
No, no, me!

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:29.530
Well, maybe it should be you, then! 
Go right on ahead!

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:37.380
<i>Wh-What have I gotten myself into?!</i>

00:08:38.370 --> 00:08:43.690
<i>Precisely. Talking about ambitious passions 
at this time of year is a bad idea because,</i>

00:08:39.060 --> 00:08:44.650
All jokes aside, unless we make some changes, 
Teiai doesn't have much of a future.

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:45.910
<i>in time, you'll potentially 
embarrass not only yourself,</i>

00:08:44.650 --> 00:08:48.040
That's right! It's all up to us.

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:48.040
<i>but those who have to listen to you.</i>

00:08:48.040 --> 00:08:50.420
Don't you agree?

00:08:51.320 --> 00:08:54.770
I-I see what you mean!

00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:58.070
<i>He's baffled, forced to 
give ambiguous responses.</i>

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:01.270
<i>What an overwhelmingly awkward situation!</i>

00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:06.800
First of all, Teiai is way 
too inefficient as is.

00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:08.360
Kikuchi?

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:15.070
Right now, there are over 100 
Teiai offices around the country.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:17.910
Check it out. There's even one way out here.

00:09:19.350 --> 00:09:23.250
The edge of Japan... The Teiai 
South Hateruma Island office.

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.260
Why on earth do we need an office there?

00:09:26.260 --> 00:09:27.700
I agree.

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:30.630
<i>No, but that's...</i>

00:09:30.630 --> 00:09:34.330
<i>That's where you guys are 
being transferred to!</i>

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:37.830
Let's propose closing it ASAP.

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:39.080
<i>Would announcement season get here already?!</i>

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:41.460
"The main office isn't the branch 
office's mother!" Like that?

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:45.270
<i>And then it finally begins.</i>

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:47.660
<i>HR starts contacting the transfers...</i>

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:49.770
<i>{sign also} The unofficial announcements!</i>

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:52.020
<b>The unofficial announcements!</b>

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.020
<i>The two weeks that decide their fates!</i>

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:54.300
<i>Psst... Psst... Psst...</i>

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:58.910
<i>By this time, news of the transfers has 
spread to everyone but the affected parties.</i>

00:09:56.900 --> 00:09:58.910
<b>Twitch... Twitch...</b>

00:09:59.090 --> 00:10:02.530
<b>Twitch... Twitch...</b>

00:09:59.510 --> 00:10:02.530
<i>An anxious ring begins to 
form around the transfers.</i>

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:06.680
This is Team Tonegawa.

00:10:09.770 --> 00:10:10.970
I understand.

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:15.050
N-Nagata-san... HR wants to talk to you.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:18.550
<b>Psst... Psst...</b>

00:10:21.410 --> 00:10:23.430
This is Nagata speaking.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:29.190
What? Me?

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:32.040
A-Are you sure it's not some kind of mistake?

00:10:36.010 --> 00:10:38.070
I see...

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:42.200
<i>Psst...</i>

00:10:47.400 --> 00:10:50.050
U-Uh, Nagata-san...

00:10:50.610 --> 00:10:53.840
I'm not sure what to say...

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:55.970
It seems...

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:00.970
There was some kind of error with my 
time card, so I need to re-submit it.

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:04.770
I could have sworn I filled 
it out right, though.

00:11:04.770 --> 00:11:05.970
<i>And it continues.</i>

00:11:05.970 --> 00:11:08.100
Hagio-san, it's for you.

00:11:09.350 --> 00:11:12.660
What? I don't have any vacation days left?

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:17.360
Sorry, Kikuchi, but I need you to move...

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:20.360
that vase.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:20.860
Yes, sir.

00:11:21.770 --> 00:11:26.280
<i>Time passes on with the trio 
unaware of their incoming news...</i>

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:31.370
<i>It's now the morning of the final 
day of announcements, in October.</i>

00:11:37.210 --> 00:11:40.010
<b>Psst...</b>

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:44.150
<i>I see. They must've finally heard.</i>

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:48.520
Yamazaki...

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:52.660
W-Well... I don't know what to say.

00:11:53.670 --> 00:11:58.150
I'm pretty sad to hear about it, too.

00:11:58.810 --> 00:11:59.650
But...

00:12:00.150 --> 00:12:05.030
The days I spent with you all as 
part of Tonegawa-sensei's team...

00:12:07.460 --> 00:12:09.490
I'll never forget...

00:12:09.490 --> 00:12:10.500
Paspo.

00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:16.170
Seems Hagio lost his Paspo card.

00:12:16.760 --> 00:12:17.920
Paspo?!

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:21.430
How much was on it?

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:24.260
A little more than 10,000 yen, I think...

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:26.360
Damn, man.

00:12:26.360 --> 00:12:28.640
That is rough.

00:12:28.640 --> 00:12:31.540
HR, would you freaking hurry it up?!

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:35.150
<i>Yamazaki's overwhelming 
feelings of vexation increase.</i>

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:38.790
<i>By the way, you can have a new 
Paspo card issued to you.</i>

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:41.300
<i>See you in the second half!</i>

00:12:42.570 --> 00:12:45.620
Like, "I'll kill you, you 
bunch of trash!" Right?

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:51.210
<i>On the last day of the transfer period in 
October, the announcement goes out.</i>

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:55.010
So, with the recent staffing changes,

00:12:55.010 --> 00:13:00.870
three of our team are going to be moving 
to the South Hateruma Island office.

00:13:01.830 --> 00:13:04.660
<i>All unofficial announcements have gone out.</i>

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:08.680
The branch office has asked 
for the kind of productivity

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:12.350
we've displayed here for their office.

00:13:13.170 --> 00:13:15.630
Each of you, go on and give your regards.

00:13:15.630 --> 00:13:16.500
Right!

00:13:17.030 --> 00:13:19.430
Everyone, we didn't work together for long,

00:13:19.430 --> 00:13:21.360
but I appreciate all the 
help you've given me.

00:13:21.360 --> 00:13:25.300
Looking back, when I was 
first moved to this team,

00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:23.940
They're calmer than I figured.

00:13:23.940 --> 00:13:26.840
Yeah. Hopefully nothing crazy happens.

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:27.360
I experienced a lot of 
anxiety and failure...

00:13:27.360 --> 00:13:28.790
This is bad.

00:13:28.430 --> 00:13:29.370
<b>Psst...</b>

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:31.730
What is?

00:13:31.730 --> 00:13:35.370
Notice anything about their expressions?

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:40.880
At a glance, they seem cheery enough, 
like they're cool with being transferred.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:43.760
But they aren't fully hiding it.

00:13:43.760 --> 00:13:46.970
You can see how dead their eyes 
are behind their sunglasses!

00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:48.970
<b>Psst...</b>

00:13:48.970 --> 00:13:54.720
<b>Psst... Psst... Psst...</b>

00:13:49.560 --> 00:13:53.050
Things are gonna get rough at 
the going-away party tonight.

00:13:54.720 --> 00:13:57.230
<b>Japanese Dining
Takumi</b>

00:13:55.810 --> 00:13:57.230
<i>That evening...</i>

00:13:57.590 --> 00:13:59.230
Cheers!

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:04.990
That's ice cold!

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:07.740
Let's drink all the way until morning.

00:14:12.390 --> 00:14:14.080
Where's Tonegawa-sensei?

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:16.910
The president called for him, 
so he's going to be late.

00:14:16.910 --> 00:14:18.500
What're you talking about?

00:14:20.170 --> 00:14:22.140
The team's in your hands now.

00:14:22.140 --> 00:14:23.100
Yeah.

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:24.210
That's right.

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:29.010
<i>Please, let this end without trouble...</i>

00:14:29.010 --> 00:14:32.610
<i>However, this round of drinks marked 
the beginning of the fireworks.</i>

00:14:32.610 --> 00:14:35.100
<i>Once they're all buzzed, it begins...</i>

00:14:37.350 --> 00:14:39.520
Yeah!

00:14:41.270 --> 00:14:43.980
Saemon, yeah!

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:46.400
Kikuchi-san, you're being too loud!

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:48.590
Let's chat, buddy.

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:49.820
Huh?

00:14:49.820 --> 00:14:53.530
We're on the same team, but we've 
never rapped about it before!

00:14:53.530 --> 00:14:54.910
Rapped about what?

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:57.790
Our big men-in-black ideas!

00:14:57.790 --> 00:15:03.130
No, I don't really do the whole 
"fill-in-the-blank ideas" thing.

00:15:03.990 --> 00:15:07.420
It always seems like it'd be 
pointless to talk about...

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.050
Or like, nonsense?

00:15:09.050 --> 00:15:13.800
<i>Dribble, dribble... Dribble, dribble...</i>

00:15:14.760 --> 00:15:16.360
K-Kikuchi-san?!

00:15:16.360 --> 00:15:19.040
ry... You're so cold, man...

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:21.560
Like a damn machine...

00:15:21.560 --> 00:15:23.560
Dry Saemon...

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:27.570
<b>Dry + Saemon =
Dryaemon</b>

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:28.170
Dryaemon!

00:15:25.690 --> 00:15:27.560
<i>The first signs are...</i>

00:15:28.170 --> 00:15:31.610
Save me, Dryaemon!

00:15:30.570 --> 00:15:33.050
<i>Those who get sloppy drunk...</i>

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:38.210
'Sup, Nagata-senpaiski?

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:39.970
Let me give you a back rub, bro.

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:42.830
Hey, your beer's empty, dude!

00:15:43.150 --> 00:15:45.520
You need a pitcher, Nagata?

00:15:45.520 --> 00:15:47.250
Give it a rest!

00:15:47.250 --> 00:15:48.410
Nagata-san?

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:52.090
This might be the last 
chance I get to say this...

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:57.310
It's awkward for me, okay?! 
You and your whole jock shtick!

00:15:57.960 --> 00:15:59.240
Nagata-sa—

00:15:59.240 --> 00:16:00.930
And the thing I really hate is how

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:05.940
every time I try to humor you, 
you act like I'm the one doesn't get it!

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:09.390
When you're the the one-note asshole!

00:16:09.390 --> 00:16:10.940
E-Easy, guys!

00:16:11.290 --> 00:16:13.380
Oh, there you go, getting physical!

00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:16.130
This is why I can't stand jocks!

00:16:16.610 --> 00:16:19.080
<i>Those who get a little too real, and...</i>

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:23.220
Good luck down there, Hagio!

00:16:22.430 --> 00:16:28.090
<b>Ogino</b>

00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:27.320
Wait, no, I'm Ogino! You're Hagio!

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:31.090
No! I'm Ogino now!

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:31.090
<b>Hagio</b>

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:35.940
<b>Hagio</b>

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.730
<i>Those who attempt to swap identities.</i>

00:16:31.640 --> 00:16:32.720
You're Hagio!

00:16:32.720 --> 00:16:33.730
But that's you!

00:16:34.170 --> 00:16:37.650
<i>Shame! Humiliation! Dishonor!</i>

00:16:35.940 --> 00:16:38.400
I'm Ogino! You gotta believe me!

00:16:37.650 --> 00:16:41.350
<i>Three distinct flavors of 
overwhelming embarrassment!</i>

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:39.600
I'm sorry, man, but no!

00:16:39.600 --> 00:16:40.330
Even our voices are similar!

00:16:39.870 --> 00:16:41.350
<b>Embarrassment!!!</b>

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:41.350
Not that similar!

00:16:41.350 --> 00:16:43.290
No one is going to buy that!

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:44.360
Damn it!

00:16:43.290 --> 00:16:45.100
Gonda-san, what should we do?

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:48.110
This is a nice bath...

00:16:50.280 --> 00:16:54.730
<i>The other men in black are engulfed 
in the flames of drunken foolishness!</i>

00:16:56.010 --> 00:16:58.240
This is really nice...

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:01.610
<i>And before long, it's total chaos!</i>

00:17:01.610 --> 00:17:04.600
Help me, Dryaemon!

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:05.880
And if I'm being honest, I hate your face!

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:08.250
Say that again, you son of a—

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:08.880
Let's all calm down!

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:10.680
Hagio! You're Hagio!

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:12.650
I am Ogino!

00:17:12.650 --> 00:17:14.740
Ogino!

00:17:15.370 --> 00:17:17.190
What lovely water...

00:17:17.760 --> 00:17:20.510
Th-This is out of control!

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:22.770
It's hell.

00:17:23.590 --> 00:17:25.270
What the hell is going on here?

00:17:25.940 --> 00:17:26.770
<b>Psst...</b>

00:17:27.190 --> 00:17:29.770
T-Tonegawa-sensei!

00:17:31.140 --> 00:17:33.640
Hey, it's Tonegawa-sensei!

00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:38.330
How's it feel? You feelin' good about 
sending us to some rinky-dink island?

00:17:38.330 --> 00:17:39.660
Kikuchi-san, stop!

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:48.660
You said all that nice stuff about us 
showing our skills at the branch office,

00:17:48.660 --> 00:17:50.920
but did you know this?!

00:17:52.760 --> 00:17:56.930
Basically all the work that the 
South Hateruma Island office does...

00:17:57.340 --> 00:18:04.350
is collect the seaweed extract that the 
president's favorite supplement is made from!

00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:08.440
All you do, all day long, is stare at a vat.

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:11.800
No project planning or execution needed!

00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:24.840
It's true. What I said this afternoon 
was the superficial take on things.

00:18:24.840 --> 00:18:26.450
It's fair to call it lip service.

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:27.760
See?!

00:18:27.760 --> 00:18:28.580
I knew it...

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:33.210
To be blunt, this transfer is half-demotion.

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:39.240
But it's half about my expectations, too.

00:18:39.700 --> 00:18:42.850
I'm sending you because I 
believe you can make it back.

00:18:45.350 --> 00:18:50.600
And you should be able to, if you 
get results and never give up.

00:18:53.110 --> 00:18:57.740
You could have your current 
position again, maybe even more.

00:18:57.740 --> 00:18:59.480
That's a load of crap!

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.360
All your smooth sailing...

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:07.120
You've never done anything but win, 
so how could you understand?!

00:19:07.890 --> 00:19:11.670
Big comebacks like that don't 
happen for normal people!

00:19:13.770 --> 00:19:16.250
We'll never make our way back up!

00:19:19.650 --> 00:19:22.390
These are your going-away gifts. Open them.

00:19:26.210 --> 00:19:30.390
Sunblock and sunglasses...

00:19:30.390 --> 00:19:33.940
The sun down there is a lot 
harsher than it is here.

00:19:34.890 --> 00:19:41.990
So you'll absolutely need sunblock, 
not to mention those UV-blocking sunglasses.

00:19:44.180 --> 00:19:45.410
UV...

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:49.120
One other thing. 
Watch yourselves in the ocean.

00:19:50.390 --> 00:19:53.120
They have coral reef snakes down there.

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:55.630
T-Tonegawa-sensei?

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:58.880
How do you know so much 
about South Hateruma Island?

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:03.130
Just a little advice from a senpai.

00:20:04.820 --> 00:20:06.760
<i>Th-That scar...</i>

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:08.600
<i>No way...</i>

00:20:16.070 --> 00:20:18.650
So that's it.

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:21.030
Tonegawa-sensei was also...

00:20:21.830 --> 00:20:25.780
We're the ones who didn't understand!

00:20:26.370 --> 00:20:29.390
It hasn't been smooth sailing after all.

00:20:29.390 --> 00:20:30.540
<i>Indeed!</i>

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:33.160
<i>At a shady business like Teiai,</i>

00:20:33.160 --> 00:20:37.700
<i>disproportionate punishment 
comes with the territory,</i>

00:20:37.700 --> 00:20:41.350
<i>no matter how talented a 
shot-caller you may be!</i>

00:20:43.680 --> 00:20:46.340
<i>But if you don't give up...</i>

00:20:46.820 --> 00:20:47.830
What's the matter?

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:50.680
Are you boys not coming to the after-party?

00:20:53.320 --> 00:20:55.260
We're with you, sir!

00:20:55.260 --> 00:20:57.780
<i>You will be rewarded!</i>

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:00.310
<i>Sometimes.</i>

00:21:01.090 --> 00:21:02.940
We're hanging in there!

00:21:04.210 --> 00:21:10.200
<i>This is the story of a lone man who 
struggles between his employer,</i>

00:21:10.200 --> 00:21:14.260
<i>the president, and his own 
employees, the men in black...</i>

00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:18.970
<i>Tonegawa Yukio: Middle Manager!</i>

00:22:54.770 --> 00:22:57.350
Next time, "Alignment."

00:22:55.990 --> 00:23:00.250
<b>Alignment</b>
